WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:05.750
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and yesterday
during my Walking Dead episode 13 video I

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.160
asked you all to submit questions about the
many WTF moments.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.019
I picked 10 of them with one bonus question.

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:14.419
Largely it seemed like the biggest questions
everyone had were Beth getting kidnapped,

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:17.130
Daryl’s new friends and Terminus.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.800
Before we get started congratulations to “melovetorun”
for being the week 5 winner of the giveaway.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.699
I’ll be messaging you on your channel for
details.

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:27.630
If you’re finding me for the first time,
just as a way to say thank you to everyone

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.109
for being so awesome I’m randomly selecting
a subscriber from the comments on my Walking

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:32.480
Dead reviews to give a $20 amazon giftcard
to.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.879
The next round will start with episode 14
on Sunday.

00:00:34.879 --> 00:00:39.059
So let’s answer some questions, there were
a lot of really good ones this week.

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:44.670
Question 1 - Andrew Jones asks do you think
that Glenn is following Maggie's trail?

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.559
Or traveling from a different direction altogether
to Terminus?

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:51.850
Yes, so it’s totally possible that those
Terminus maps are all over the place, it’s

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.739
hard to guess where Glenn was the last time
we saw him, but in my head I think everyone

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:01.550
either went east or west using the railroad
tracks and Abraham was headed north east.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.850
It’s hard to guess which way Maggie went
when they left the prison but I think the

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.770
show wants us to think he’s coming from
behind her.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.470
So that’s what I’m going to choose to
believe.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.953
Circumstances seem like they’re slowing
causing all of the groups to converge at the

00:01:13.953 --> 00:01:15.720
Terminus by the end of the season.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.910
Question 2 - Alan Michael asks Who do you
think is in Terminus?

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:24.810
Just because the word Sanctuary appears almost
every time they’re talking about it I’m

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.650
choosing to believe it’s the Sanctuary from
the comic books.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.960
Which means if they’re doing a direct adaptation
it would be Negan and The Saviors.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.430
But none of the writers or cast has mentioned
him, so it’s possible that they’re messing

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.710
with the story just a little bit.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.670
There’s also the introduction of Daryl’s
new buddies and the Gareth character that

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:41.970
was announced last year.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.580
We still haven’t met him.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.320
So assuming the show sticks to it’s comic
book guns, let’s just say Saviors or the

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.460
closest possible thing if they decide not
to use that name.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.930
Either way it’s bad, very bad.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:57.300
Question 3 - Carolina Aimee asks What did
you think those Daryl/Beth moments throughout

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.920
the whole episode meant?

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.680
Do you think he will be the one that rescues/finds
her?﻿

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.510
That awkward pause that Daryl and Beth had
was because she was trying to get him to admit

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.149
that he’d started to believe good things
were still possible.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:13.310
And what he didn’t say or said with a shrug
was that it was because Beth had started to

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.450
rub off on him.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:18.940
The awkward pause itself did kind of make
it seem like there was some implied sexual

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.519
attraction, but I don’t think Daryl sees
it that way.

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:23.569
I think he just cares about her a lot.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:31.450
More than he’s willing to say out loud.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.150
Question 4 - TheMouseNetwork asks is Gareth
the person that took Beth in the car?

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.849
Or Someone else?

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:41.269
So one of the biggest theories about Beth’s
mystery kidnapper is that it’s one person

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:43.549
and it’s the new Gareth character.

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:47.560
Who is a version of the Reverend Gabriel character
from the comic books.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.599
In that story he was accused of being involved
with the kidnapping of Dale.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:53.480
Which turned out to be The Hunters.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:03:02.090
There is a rumor that Gareth is tied to the
Terminus, so I’d say the he was either the

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:07.930
one who abducted her or he was orchestrating
it.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:13.490
Question 5 - Matthew I asks Do you think anyone
will make it to Terminus before the season

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:17.930
finale or do you think everyone makes it to
terminus in season finale?

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:23.139
l definitely think most of the cast will make
it to Terminus, there has been so much foreshadowing

00:03:23.139 --> 00:03:28.040
in the last couple of episodes it would be
a huge audience burn on us if we never actually

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.040
got to see it.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.920
They didn’t make it explicit in the episode,
but I also think that Joes’ group, the one’s

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.120
Daryl ran into are tied to Terminus too.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:44.489
Question 6 - MrPixel64 asks Do you think those
guys will help Daryl to find the car/Beth?﻿

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:49.709
They seem pretty terrible so I’ll say no,
but based on everyone slowly being herded

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:52.610
toward the Terminus I think he’ll find her
coincidentally.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.610
Alone with everyone else.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.359
I’m really interested to see how each group
is introduced to the community that already

00:03:57.359 --> 00:03:58.359
lives there.

00:03:58.359 --> 00:04:00.250
If it’s going to be like their introduction
to Woodbury.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.519
I have a feeling that because Joe’s group
views Daryl as a kindred spirit, they’ll

00:04:04.519 --> 00:04:05.519
vouch for him.

00:04:05.519 --> 00:04:07.540
They still give off this murdery vibe.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.319
So I don’t think he’s any safer than everyone
else.

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:15.219
Question 7 - Liv Taylor asks How in the world
did Daryl let those guys just sneak up on

00:04:15.219 --> 00:04:16.489
him like that?﻿

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.810
I think he had just hit a new bottom.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.470
Like spending all that time with Beth had
made him really happy and hopeful again and

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:27.030
then losing her and being on his own and lost
made him die a little inside.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.470
Or die a little more.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:33.160
He really just gave up for a little while
and given that they ran into him I think geographically,

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.410
all of the groups are a lot closer than we
think.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:39.390
Because Joe was just at that house where Rick,
Michonne and Carl were.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:43.900
Question 8 - Phimackphil asks do you Think
the Gareth character is going to be a cliffhanger?

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.030
I assume you’re talking about either the
next episode or the season finale.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.440
I think we’ll meet him before the finale.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.040
There are really only 3 more episodes left,
so I don’t think the show will go on any

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.280
crazy tangents with the exception of whatever
the cliffhanger is for next season.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.850
The teaser for the next episode makes it seem
like it will mostly revolve around Carol and

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:01.850
Tyreese’s group.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:05.410
We haven’t seen Rick’s group in a couple
episodes and given that we’ve seen Beth

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:10.260
and Daryl for the last two weeks, I don’t
think we’ll meet Gareth until episode 15.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.540
The show has been doing this weird thing where
it focuses on the same characters for a couple

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:18.100
episodes, then jumps to other groups for a
couple episodes, so I expect that trend to

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.230
continue in the next episode.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.710
Jumping to characters we didn’t see this
week.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:27.190
Question 9 - Demik Holdat (no avatar) asks
Do you think that Daryl laying down on the

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:29.000
funeral bed was a sign?

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.190
I hope not, Daryl isn’t in the comic books,
so you can’t really say he’s living on

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:37.610
borrowed time.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:40.560
There are a couple characters that are dead
in the comic books, but still alive on the

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.560
show.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.000
I’d put them higher up on the list of potential
deaths.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:50.400
There’s always the potential that someone
could die trying to save Beth.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.560
But that doesn’t necessarily mean it will
be Daryl.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.480
I haven’t seen any quotes from Norman Reedus,
but I do wonder if he ad libbed jumping in

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.360
the coffin or if the writers wrote it in the
script.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.620
Question 10 - Amy Haines asks If Bob had really
been bit do you not think he would have shown

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:09.390
at least some signs or even shown panic whenever
Sasha or Maggie were not around?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.930
He did say that the Walker grazed his bandage,
so either he’s telling the truth and walker

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:20.640
teeth did not touch his flesh or he’s ignoring
that warning sign that Sasha talked about.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.150
One of the things I really liked about the
episode was how ambiguous it was with the

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.070
character’s lives.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.320
Everyone almost died at some point.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.230
The writers are doing a really good job of
teasing a big death.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.690
Which I still believe is coming.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.570
Most likely in the finale.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:40.190
Bonus Question - Marion Swanson asks Do you
think the show actually made a mistake by

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:44.380
displaying Abraham's group so faithfully?

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.340
So this is actually a carry-over question
from two episodes ago, but I saw a lot of

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:53.440
other people commenting on the appearance
of Abraham and Rosita specifically.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.330
Mostly that Abraham was a little too out of
shape and Rosita was a little too much of

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.720
a Barbie Doll.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:03.330
I didn’t really mind Abraham’s appearance,
but I did think Rosita seemed a little out

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.810
of place with the booty shorts.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.820
I guess in the apocalypse you just have to
do whatever you can to feel comfortable.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.300
I think it would be a bigger issue if she
had more time on screen.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:16.560
I don’t begrudge little things like that
unless a show forces me to stare at something

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:17.710
all the time.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.190
So thank you guys so much for submitting questions.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.430
This was a lot of fun as always.

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:25.680
Two big things we can look forward to in the
next couple of episodes are meeting Gareth

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.730
and seeing the Terminus.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.410
Next week it looks like Lizzie and Mika’s
are in for major trouble.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.760
Be sure to subscribe to get my video.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.260
I’ll post it right after the episode airs.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.880
I’m also posting a breakdown of the Game
of Thrones trailer later tonight.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:44.930
Right now click here for my top 5 WTF moments
from the episode and click here for that breakdown

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:45.930
video.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:46.930
Thanks for watching, see you guys in a little
bit.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:47.139
High Fives!

